<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12183" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cynŏsūra</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κυνόσουρα</span>
		(hound's-tail). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The constellation at the north pole, the
			Cynosura</i>, or <i>Lesser Bear</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 2, 20, 66</span></i>; id.
			poët. N. D. 2, 41, 105 and 106;
				<i><span class="en">Caes. Germ. Arat. 187</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 3,
				107 al.</span></i>—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cynŏsūris</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f.
			<i>adj., of</i> or <i>pertaining to the
				Cynosura</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ursa,</span>”
				<i>the Lesser Bear</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 5, 3, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cauda,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes. Germ. Arat. 189</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A town in Arcadia</i>, <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 4,
				295</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
